    "description": "3Y annual year-on-year inflation cap priced with QuantLib's Black-76 formula on QuantLib reference indices and discount factors.",
    "domain": "rates.inflation_cap_floor",
    "last_reviewed_by": "finstack-quant",
    "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-24",
    "name": "usd_yoy_inflation_cap_black_quantlib",
    "regen_command": "uv run python -m scripts.golden.quantlib.generate --product yoy_inflation_cap_black",
    "review_interval_months": 6,
    "screenshots": [],
    "source": "quantlib",
    "source_detail": "QuantLib 1.43 supplies the reference indices (CPI.laggedFixing on a ZeroInflationIndex with a flat annually compounded Act/365F ZeroInflationCurve, three-month lag, CPI.Linear), the FlatForward discount factors and the blackFormula optionlet value. QuantLib's year-on-year cap/floor engines forecast from a separate year-on-year curve instead of the zero-index ratio, so the generator assembles the strip itself: forward rate (I_end / I_start - 1) / accrual with 30/360 accruals, flat volatility, and Act/365F option time from the valuation date to the lagged end reference date. DV01, Inflation01 and vega are central differences for one basis point of the nominal zero rate, one basis point of the zero-inflation rate and one volatility point.",
